Z||000001||Kasdan||10-31-2001||01:09 PM||||Sootah, yes my rebuilt Fiero 2.8 Longblock cost me $1300 with a 36month/36k mile warranty.  I purchased my motor from a local company here in Athens called Legett motors.  of course there was a core charge, so i guess the motor was really around 1k-1100.  They even picked up my old block for me.  Included was an "install kit"  which incuded a few sorted gaskets, half of which didnt fit, so be sure you get the right gaskets.  My car sounds like crap right now, because i think the shop cracked my rear manifold, and i have a clogged cat so my manifolds light up the compartment like a night fire.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">               <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt motor with &gt;100 miles, Double wiper blades(12hp), Red LED's(10hp), Dragon sticker(15hp), yellow calipers (7 hp), Grant wheel(30hp), pine tree(75hp)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986<p>[This message has been edited by Kasdan (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||1
